            <fr:title text="iota builds indices without a constant">iota builds indices without a constant</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404866570</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>What do <html:code><![CDATA[iota(), iota_dimension=1]]></html:code> and <html:code><![CDATA[constant({...})]]></html:code> do in <fr:link href="/NO8J/" title="HLO" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/NO8J/" display-uri="NO8J" type="local">HLO</fr:link>?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:code>iota</html:code> generates <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0, 1, 2, \ldots ]]></fr:tex> along the given dimension and is constant across the others. It is how <html:code>arange</html:code>, index comparisons, and position-dependent masks appear — a causal attention mask is an <html:code>iota</html:code> on rows compared against an <html:code>iota</html:code> on columns.

  <html:strong>The point is that it materialises nothing.</html:strong> A mask built from <html:code>iota</html:code> is computed inside the consuming kernel, so it fuses (<fr:link href="/ZUYH/" title="A fusion op is a kernel launch boundary" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/ZUYH/" display-uri="ZUYH" type="local">A <fr:link href="/38CM/" title="Operator fusion" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/38CM/" display-uri="38CM" type="local">fusion</fr:link> op is a kernel launch boundary</fr:link>) and never occupies <fr:link href="/AI2G/" title="High bandwidth memory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/AI2G/" display-uri="AI2G" type="local">High bandwidth memory</fr:link>. The same mask written as a literal would be a constant the size of the attention matrix, read from memory every step.

  <html:code>constant</html:code> embeds a literal, and a large one is elided in the text dump as <html:code><![CDATA[{...}]]></html:code> — present in the module, dropped from the printout, the same courtesy <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link> extends with <html:code>dense_resource</html:code> (<fr:link href="/5B7I/" title="A scalar inside dense is a splat" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5B7I/" display-uri="5B7I" type="local">A scalar inside dense is a splat</fr:link>).
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
