            <fr:title text="A fusion op is a kernel launch boundary">A <fr:link href="/38CM/" title="Operator fusion" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/38CM/" display-uri="38CM" type="local">fusion</fr:link> op is a kernel launch boundary</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404870845</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>What is a <html:code>fusion</html:code> instruction in <fr:link href="/NO8J/" title="HLO" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/NO8J/" display-uri="NO8J" type="local">HLO</fr:link> and where is its body?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:pre><html:code class="language-llvm"><![CDATA[%fusion.2 = f32[8,128]{1,0} fusion(f32[8,128]{1,0} %p0, f32[128]{0} %p1),
            kind=kLoop, calls=%fused_computation.2]]></html:code></html:pre>

  The body is a separate computation named by <html:code>calls=</html:code>, printed elsewhere in the module; its parameters line up positionally with the fusion's operands (<fr:link href="/W9HX/" title="parameter(i) is positional" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/W9HX/" display-uri="W9HX" type="local">parameter(i) is positional</fr:link>).

  <html:strong>The fusion op is the kernel launch boundary.</html:strong> Everything inside the body runs in one kernel, with intermediates staying in registers instead of round-tripping to <fr:link href="/AI2G/" title="High bandwidth memory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/AI2G/" display-uri="AI2G" type="local">High bandwidth memory</fr:link> — that is the whole point of <fr:link href="/38CM/" title="Operator fusion" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/38CM/" display-uri="38CM" type="local">Operator fusion</fr:link>.

  It is therefore the unit that matters for performance work: a name in a profile is a fusion name, and the question "why is this slow" is usually "what ended up inside this body, and what did not". <html:code>kind=</html:code> says which emitter generated it (<fr:link href="/L148/" title="The fusion kind names the emitter" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/L148/" display-uri="L148" type="local">The <fr:link href="/38CM/" title="Operator fusion" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/38CM/" display-uri="38CM" type="local">fusion</fr:link> kind names the emitter</fr:link>).
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
